  message: "CORRECTION TO THE PRECEDING MESSAGE. One sentence in it is blank where three\nnames should be -- I passed the text through a double-quoted shell argument and\nthe backticked identifiers were command-substituted away. Edit-mode is\nhuman-gated, so the sentence is restored here rather than repaired in place:\n\n  \"THE SPLIT IS EXACTLY THE NAMING CONVENTION, so the residual is precise rather\n   than estimated. The heuristic requires a name starting with New, longer than\n   three characters, with an uppercase fourth character. New and Default are\n   neither, so gin.Default(), fiber.New() and echo.New() are untouched and still\n   inert.\"\n\nNothing else in that message is affected; the measured numbers and the\nsix-of-seven residual stand as written."  # df6f
