  message: "SEQUENCING NOTE 2026-09-03, from the owner's \"all at once\" question. Two\npreconditions this item's own description implied now have owners:\n\n  WI-sovup   L4 corpus coverage: kotlin and objc have NO repo on disk, swift\n             and scala one each (VernissageServer, docspell). Rows for those\n             four cannot be admitted by measurement until it lands.\n  WI-higob    INV-dihos Phase 6: swift + objc never got a registry consumer;\n             WI-hijot (P4) is scala's. Rows for those three ship present-and-\n             dead until the consumer exists.\n\nConsumers for the other six after the current L2/L3 queue: go (WI-doluf,\ndone), rust (WI-titor + WI-papar), java (WI-gajuh), python (WI-hudam /\nINV-mumov / WI-makij / INV-luhug), kotlin + javascript (WI-nasuf).\n\nSHAPE DECISION SHOULD COME FIRST. Whichever of those consumers is built next\nshould read the registry through the interface THIS item's loader will feed\n(qualified type, keyed the way the per-language registries already are), or\nthe wiring gets redone when the rows land. Recorded so the java work under\nWI-gajuh starts from that interface rather than inventing one.\n\nIf the rows are written for all nine languages in one pass, keep one\nmeasurement arm per language and merge per language where possible, so a\nprecision-band trip after the merge has a name on it (0012's own caveat: \"no\nA/B was run, so no fix is attributed\"). Rows a fixture proves no analyzer\nconsumes must carry a consumed_by status the drift guard can read."  # cdb3
