- op: discuss  # 863c
  at: '2026-09-04T13:29:00Z'  # 863c
  by: agent  # 863c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 863c
  clock: 9  # 863c
  nonce: 863c  # 863c
  message: "SHIPPED, AND THE ITEM'S HEADLINE CLAIM DOES NOT SURVIVE ITS OWN MEASUREMENT. Both are\npart of the deliverable.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. A `library_signatures` catalogue family (loader, rows for go / java / objc /\npython / swift, a `CatalogSpec` with `user_channel=\"library_signatures.d\"` because rows\ndescribe LIBRARIES and an in-house factory returning an in-house type is exactly the row a\nuser has), merged into the SAME return-type registry the analyzers already read, with\n`setdefault` AFTER the analysed rows so an in-repo declaration always beats a catalogue\nguess. No new resolution path, exactly as this item's shape ruling required.\n\nTHREE CORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEM'S OWN PLAN, each found by reading the code rather than the\nplan:\n\n1. THE MERGE IS FOUR PLACES, NOT ONE. `analyze_go` and `analyze_objc` are standalone\n   functions with their own aggregations, and `java.py` builds its registry from\n   `Symbol.meta[\"return_type\"]`, not from `FileAnalysis.method_return_types` at all. A\n   name-filtered grep found three of the four -- objc calls its variable\n   `_method_return_types` -- so the enumeration has to be by what the code DOES\n   (`.method_return_types.items()`), not by variable name.\n2. GO NEEDED A LOOKUP, NOT JUST A MERGE. Its registry is consulted for a BARE call and for\n   a method on a TYPED variable. A package-qualified producer -- `net.Listen(...)`,\n   `exec.Command(...)` -- takes the selector branch, where `net` is a package rather than a\n   variable, so `func_vars.get(\"net\")` is empty and the registry was never asked. The\n   catalogue merge ALONE left `ln.Accept()` and `c.Start()` on the `external` sentinel,\n   which is precisely the inertness this item was filed for.\n3. JAVA'S ROWS MUST ARRIVE ALREADY QUALIFIED, because its loop qualifies each ANALYSED\n   return type against the DECLARING FILE's imports and a catalogue row has no declaring\n   file.\n\nTHE CLAIM THAT FAILED. io-boundaries are IDENTICAL between arms, both cold, on all five\nrepositories: caddy 299, gocryptfs 253, guacamole-client 93, AFNetworking 15, Alamofire 40.\nTraced on a minimal fixture: `ln, _ := net.Listen(...); ln.Accept()` ALREADY produces a\n`net_recv` chain with no library row at all, though the analyzer emits `go:external`.\nSomething downstream already recovers it, so \"these rows unlock catalogue rows that cannot\notherwise match\" is FALSE for the stdlib rows shipped here.\n\nA NEAR-MISS WORTH RECORDING: the first A/B appeared to show the rows creating those\nboundaries. It did not -- `io-boundaries` does not re-run the analyzer and that run reused\na cached behavior map (the standing landmine, hit by omitting `cache-clear` from an ad-hoc\nrun that the rig does perform). Re-run cold, the arms are equal.\n\nTHE CLAIM THAT HOLDS, with every moved row read back and 0 regressions in either repo:\n    caddy      typed module slots 7,271 -> 7,314;  43 sites external -> typed\n    gocryptfs  typed module slots 3,734 -> 4,009; 274 sites external -> typed\n               (`external` bucket 704 -> 429, a 39% reduction)\n    191 os (`file.Truncate(0)`), 81 os/exec (`cmd.CombinedOutput()`), 19 net\n    (`conn.Close()`), 17 os (`f.Close()`), 5 os/exec (`cmd.Run()`), 2 io (`stdinPipe.Close()`)\n\nBecause io does not move while 317 sites gain a real module, the classifier was ALREADY\nmatching these by short name. The gain is PRECISION, not recall: a match that rested on\nthe name `Close` matching some catalogued `Close` now rests on the receiver's package. The\nrecall claim in this item's filing is not supported by this cohort and should not be\nrepeated without a repository where the short-name gate refuses.\n\nDOWNSTREAM: INV-muhij's named blocker is removed -- its exact fixture now emits\n`go:os/exec:0-0:Start` and `go:os/exec:0-0:StdoutPipe`. The seven inert framework rows this\nitem measured (gin / fiber / echo) are THIRD-PARTY and belong in an ADR-0047 community\noverlay, filed separately rather than folded in.\n\nLab: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lalot_libsigs_09042026/ (DESIGN.md carries the four\ncorrections, both empirical key-shape validations, and the read-back)."  # 863c
